## On-disk format implementations

The filesystem drivers in this tree implement **published on-disk formats**.
A format is a specification — field offsets, field widths, checksum
algorithms, the shape of a directory entry — and implementing one is not
copying a program that implements it.

Every driver here was written against the format's documentation.  Where a
description refers to a reference program, it is because that program's
observable behaviour is what the format's documentation leaves ambiguous, and
the reference is to the *behaviour* (what is written to a disk, what is refused)
rather than to any source code.

No source code from another operating system's kernel, and no code from any
GPL-licensed project, is present in this tree.

